WEBVTT

00:00.350 --> 00:04.035
In nuclear engineering, an assertion is not enough.

00:04.035 --> 00:12.325
Reviewers need to know which requirement supports it, which revision applies
and how the evidence connects through design

00:12.325 --> 00:15.088
substantiation, operating constraints and controlled records.

00:15.088 --> 00:18.773
That evidence remains the responsibility of authorised specialists.

00:18.773 --> 00:27.524
Cortessa is designed to help them investigate a bounded document estate,
surface documentary questions and return to the source,

00:27.524 --> 00:32.590
without becoming the design authority, the safety assessor or the regulator.

00:33.590 --> 00:40.137
A controlled plant modification or safety-case change can connect
requirements, calculations, design descriptions, operating rules,

00:40.137 --> 00:42.319
referenced standards and revision histories.

00:42.319 --> 00:47.994
Each source has an owner, status and defined role in the approval process.

00:47.994 --> 00:55.850
The practical challenge is reconstructing the chain: what wording supports the
assertion, whether the cited document is present,

00:55.850 --> 01:03.270
whether a reference has been superseded and whether apparently similar terms
mean the same thing in context.

01:04.270 --> 01:12.092
Cortessa's target nuclear-site deployment gives each authorised specialist a
dedicated, self-sufficient box inside the site boundary.

01:12.092 --> 01:18.448
Local documents, ingestion, index, on-device model and source viewer remain on
that box.

01:18.448 --> 01:22.848
Audit and Ask run locally against the approved corpus.

01:22.848 --> 01:26.759
Author remains in development and requires further testing.

01:26.759 --> 01:35.070
The specialist controls the working context and remains responsible for design
intent, applicability and every approved revision.

01:36.070 --> 01:44.123
Specialist boxes are designed to connect through design, configuration and
independent-assurance departmental nodes to an on-site hub.

01:44.123 --> 01:51.228
The complete exchange stays inside the air-gapped site, and selected
cross-department sharing requires explicit authority.

01:51.228 --> 01:56.438
This is the target site architecture, not a deployed production-network claim.

01:56.438 --> 02:03.544
The offline revision contract and application foundations exist; authenticated
transport, key operations, scheduling, backup, recovery,

02:03.544 --> 02:06.859
site assurance and rollout remain deployment work.

02:06.859 --> 02:12.070
Cortessa does not connect to plant control or take operational action.

02:13.070 --> 02:16.801
Audit is the centre of the Cortessa workflow.

02:16.801 --> 02:24.730
It works across the selected nuclear evidence chain rather than waiting for
one question at a time.

02:24.730 --> 02:30.794
It can surface stale references, supersession questions, terminology
differences and missing documentary links.

02:30.794 --> 02:37.790
Each candidate enters authorised review; it is not automatically a safety,
compliance or licence finding.

02:38.790 --> 02:43.587
Every audit result leads back to the passages that created it.

02:43.587 --> 02:50.564
The authorised specialist can open the source, inspect surrounding wording and
confirm document state and context.

02:50.564 --> 02:55.796
If evidence is absent, Cortessa can refuse rather than fill the gap.

02:55.796 --> 03:03.645
The authorised reviewer decides whether the discrepancy is genuine, material,
already resolved or outside scope, then records the

03:03.645 --> 03:05.825
outcome through the established process.

03:05.825 --> 03:09.750
Verified shows provenance; it does not establish safety significance.

03:10.750 --> 03:16.477
Safety significance, design intent and regulatory applicability require
qualified human judgement.

03:16.477 --> 03:23.765
The licensee, design authority and independent assurance functions retain
their established responsibilities and separation.

03:23.765 --> 03:29.491
Cortessa can make the evidence route and uncertainty easier to inspect.

03:29.491 --> 03:40.424
It does not approve a modification, validate a safety case, discharge a
licence condition or certify that an argument is adequate.

03:40.424 --> 03:45.630
Formal decisions and approvals remain in the organisation's controlled
systems.

03:46.630 --> 03:54.119
A specialist-approved revision can carry signed identity, content hash, parent
lineage and approved audit context through its

03:54.119 --> 03:57.643
departmental node and, where authorised, the on-site hub.

03:57.643 --> 04:05.131
Conflicts and missing ancestry remain explicit; the hub cannot publish
specialist approval or choose the governing revision.

04:05.131 --> 04:10.858
Receipt does not certify a document or make it current or searchable
automatically.

04:10.858 --> 04:13.941
The receiving specialist governs import and use.

04:13.941 --> 04:21.430
The local Ledger supports inspection of activity but does not replace nuclear
records, approvals or independent assessment.

04:22.430 --> 04:26.650
Compare matched tasks against the existing review baseline.

04:26.650 --> 04:36.146
Measure time to reconstruct an agreed assertion-to-source chain, time to
locate the current revision, reviewer effort, cited candidate

04:36.146 --> 04:40.894
findings, specialist agreement, appropriate refusals and sampled source-path
reproducibility.

04:40.894 --> 04:45.114
Include absent evidence, difficult revisions and ambiguous terminology.

04:45.114 --> 04:48.279
Record corpus preparation and setup effort.

04:48.279 --> 04:58.830
The result should identify useful support, failure modes and remediation
before any decision about a larger corpus or another workflow.

04:59.830 --> 05:02.338
Bring one cleared change pack.

05:02.338 --> 05:11.871
Agree the specialists, baseline and evidence standard, then test the route
from local evidence work to governed departmental revision

05:11.871 --> 05:12.372
exchange.

05:12.372 --> 05:19.898
Cortessa claims no nuclear deployment, completed site rollout, regulatory
approval, safety-case acceptance or safety outcome.

05:19.898 --> 05:25.416
The architecture must be demonstrated and assured in a representative
environment.

05:25.416 --> 05:29.430
Start a conversation about a scoped nuclear evaluation.
